WEBVTT

00:00:19.603 --> 00:00:22.147
Thank you very much for your purchase!

00:00:22.147 --> 00:00:25.734
If you have the time,
please come see our afternoon show!

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:28.403
We'll be performing the B-side track!

00:00:29.738 --> 00:00:33.450
It's quite interesting to see
the actual faces of our fans.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:35.327
Thank you very much!

00:00:35.327 --> 00:00:37.538
Ino's popular among men and women of all ages.

00:00:38.497 --> 00:00:41.834
Hemo's popular among the young men and women.

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:43.293
This is embarrassing...

00:00:43.293 --> 00:00:46.255
Hayu's really popular among
young girls and middle-aged men.

00:00:46.255 --> 00:00:47.840
Thank you very much.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:50.717
Nina is popular among men in general.

00:00:52.094 --> 00:00:53.470
And Roko...

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.389
--Roko, look over here!
--So cute!

00:00:55.389 --> 00:00:57.683
She's popular among women
in their 20's and above.

00:00:57.683 --> 00:00:59.059
I knew that!

00:02:38.784 --> 00:02:40.702
"Dance and Shine!"

00:02:40.702 --> 00:02:42.454
"Dance and Shine!"
Dance and Shine!

00:02:42.454 --> 00:02:44.039
"Dance and Shine!"

00:02:56.468 --> 00:02:58.679
That's a relief for now.

00:02:58.679 --> 00:03:02.724
I'm glad Miss Hoho found
a bathroom close to the stage!

00:03:02.724 --> 00:03:06.770
The morning half went great, so now I
have to keep it up for the afternoon show!

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:10.274
But I wonder if I could go again
right before the show...

00:03:10.274 --> 00:03:13.569
Or else I'll face tragedy
like I did last time...

00:03:13.569 --> 00:03:16.697
Shoot! I have to hurry back and get ready!

00:03:20.158 --> 00:03:21.577
Everyone...?

00:03:24.663 --> 00:03:26.081
U-Um!

00:03:26.081 --> 00:03:29.209
I completely forgot to
turn on the sound muffler...

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:31.962
Oh, don't worry, we just came in.

00:03:31.962 --> 00:03:34.464
Yeah! We didn't hear anything!

00:03:34.464 --> 00:03:36.884
P-Plus, it's a natural phenomenon.

00:03:36.884 --> 00:03:38.552
Don't worry about it!

00:03:38.552 --> 00:03:40.387
Ino-<i>sempai</i>...!

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:44.892
"Lady etiquette"

00:03:45.184 --> 00:03:49.104
So what's this? Are you all
getting nervous, too?

00:03:49.104 --> 00:03:50.856
No, we're not like you.

00:03:50.856 --> 00:03:54.526
We didn't want to, but Hoho insisted.

00:03:54.526 --> 00:03:57.529
She didn't want us to
listen in on a conversation.

00:03:58.864 --> 00:04:01.658
Debt... loans... impossible to repay...

00:04:01.658 --> 00:04:05.454
That's it... My life is over. Game over...

00:04:05.454 --> 00:04:07.539
Thanks for everything...

00:04:07.539 --> 00:04:08.999
It's been fun.

00:04:08.999 --> 00:04:10.459
We shall meet again...

00:04:10.459 --> 00:04:11.710
At the hot springs...

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:13.462
--A-A-Are you okay, Miss Hoho?!
--At that land...

00:04:13.462 --> 00:04:14.588
--A-A-Are you okay, Miss Hoho?!
--A strong...

00:04:14.588 --> 00:04:17.341
A new game... Hope...

00:04:17.341 --> 00:04:18.634
Starting tomorrow...

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:23.222
...we may not eat meat ever again!

00:04:23.222 --> 00:04:25.057
Wh-What are you talking about?!

00:04:25.057 --> 00:04:26.934
Why talk about this in the bathroom?!

00:04:26.934 --> 00:04:27.601
"Fruit Tart for Life"
Why talk about this in the bathroom?!

00:04:27.601 --> 00:04:29.561
"Fruit Tart for Life"
I'm here!

00:04:29.561 --> 00:04:31.313
"Fruit Tart for Life"
What's going on?

00:04:32.898 --> 00:04:34.274
Actually...

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:38.153
I got a call from one of our higher-ups...

00:04:38.153 --> 00:04:42.157
If we don't sell at least 1,000 copies of
the CD today, things are going to be tough.

00:04:42.157 --> 00:04:43.408
What?!

00:04:43.408 --> 00:04:45.661
A-A thousand copies?!

00:04:45.661 --> 00:04:49.206
Th-That's why you don't produce 3,000 copies
on an independent label!

00:04:49.206 --> 00:04:51.208
It's "three thousand" in English!

00:04:51.208 --> 00:04:53.001
Wh-Why English?

00:04:53.001 --> 00:04:54.503
--It sounds strong!
--What?!

00:04:54.503 --> 00:04:56.880
So how many have we sold so far?

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:00.551
W-We've sold 500 in the morning half...

00:05:00.551 --> 00:05:02.219
So that means we're halfway there!

00:05:02.219 --> 00:05:03.303
That's right!

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:04.638
But...

00:05:05.597 --> 00:05:10.394
Merch sales slow down the later it gets...

00:05:10.394 --> 00:05:13.021
The hardcore fans have
been here since the morning

00:05:13.021 --> 00:05:16.775
and already bought a bunch of merch...

00:05:16.775 --> 00:05:18.527
That's true...

00:05:18.527 --> 00:05:22.698
Well, it might be different if you
added a new perk or something.

00:05:25.367 --> 00:05:27.286
What can we do?

00:05:29.204 --> 00:05:30.914
Stare...

00:05:30.914 --> 00:05:33.417
Wh-Why is everyone looking at me?!

00:05:33.417 --> 00:05:34.751
--I see.
--Yes!

00:05:34.751 --> 00:05:36.044
That's an idea!

00:05:36.044 --> 00:05:39.173
W-We can't do that to our fans!

00:05:39.173 --> 00:05:42.301
We can't add a perk to the afternoon half only!

00:05:42.301 --> 00:05:44.219
An unexpectedly valid point!

00:05:44.219 --> 00:05:47.681
The more hardcore they are,
the earlier they arrived this morning!

00:05:47.681 --> 00:05:49.600
Y-You're totally right!

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:50.893
Y-Yeah!

00:05:50.893 --> 00:05:53.937
We need to go for a frontal attack!

00:05:53.937 --> 00:05:56.773
Kick it up a notch so they'll buy a lot!

00:05:56.773 --> 00:05:58.525
That's the only way!

00:05:58.525 --> 00:06:03.614
But how could we kick things up a notch?

00:06:03.614 --> 00:06:05.199
Good question...

00:06:05.199 --> 00:06:06.617
Nina! Tone!

00:06:06.617 --> 00:06:09.161
Let's execute the frontal attack!

00:06:09.161 --> 00:06:10.913
We have to be resourceful!

00:06:10.913 --> 00:06:12.706
What are you expecting exactly?!

00:06:12.706 --> 00:06:15.000
N-Now I'm involved?!

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.668
But come to think of it...

00:06:16.668 --> 00:06:21.673
We never thought of ways
to fire up the crowd during our shows.

00:06:21.673 --> 00:06:24.927
We were all caught up trying to
perform the song earlier, too.

00:06:24.927 --> 00:06:28.388
We may need more training as idols...

00:06:28.388 --> 00:06:29.890
Training, huh?

00:06:29.890 --> 00:06:33.393
All we did was watch Cream Anmitsu's concert...

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:35.646
Um, I've got an idea!

00:06:35.646 --> 00:06:38.774
Why don't we incorporate more call and response?

00:06:38.774 --> 00:06:39.608
Huh?

00:06:39.608 --> 00:06:44.196
That's how Cream Anmitsu
fired up their fans, too.

00:06:44.196 --> 00:06:45.072
That's it!

00:06:45.072 --> 00:06:48.283
Um... What exactly is "call and response"?

00:06:48.283 --> 00:06:49.535
What?!

00:06:50.994 --> 00:06:54.206
How exactly... do you do that?

00:06:54.206 --> 00:06:56.250
For example...

00:06:57.584 --> 00:06:59.086
Well, you know...

00:06:59.086 --> 00:07:01.964
It's like immersing in each other's voices

00:07:01.964 --> 00:07:04.716
and feeling a lot of pleasure from it.

00:07:05.968 --> 00:07:07.427
Ino-<i>sempai</i>...

00:07:07.427 --> 00:07:11.014
So... why don't we give it a try?

00:07:12.015 --> 00:07:13.016
Enough!

00:07:13.016 --> 00:07:16.228
You're not wrong, but it's not that moody!

00:07:16.228 --> 00:07:17.312
Moody?

00:07:17.312 --> 00:07:21.483
You know, it's more like calling out
"let's go," "yeah," and things like that.

00:07:21.483 --> 00:07:24.069
Oh, I know what that is!

00:07:24.069 --> 00:07:25.487
Y-Yeah!

00:07:25.487 --> 00:07:28.365
It was short and sweet at the
Cream Anmitsu concert, remember?

00:07:28.365 --> 00:07:29.241
You're right!

00:07:29.241 --> 00:07:32.119
They had a great rapport with their fans!

00:07:32.119 --> 00:07:32.536
"Cream Anmitsu"
They had a great rapport with their fans!

00:07:32.536 --> 00:07:34.872
"Cream Anmitsu"
Thanks for coming out today!

00:07:34.872 --> 00:07:37.666
Hey, everyone! Are you all ready?!

00:07:37.666 --> 00:07:40.669
I'll be abusing you all again today!

00:07:40.669 --> 00:07:43.630
Yeah!

00:07:44.882 --> 00:07:46.175
Short and sweet?

00:07:46.175 --> 00:07:50.929
But if this were the case, we should've
asked Chiko for more advice.

00:07:50.929 --> 00:07:53.390
Then let's ask her.

00:07:53.390 --> 00:07:54.266
No way!

00:07:54.266 --> 00:07:57.936
Chiko's a popular idol,
how could she be available...?

00:08:07.738 --> 00:08:09.364
Chiko... seriously...

00:08:09.364 --> 00:08:12.367
N-No! Don't get creeped out, big sister.

00:08:12.367 --> 00:08:15.370
I just came to secretly support you.

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:18.749
Then this happened and I couldn't get out.

00:08:18.749 --> 00:08:20.834
Were you listening to everything, then?!

00:08:20.834 --> 00:08:22.836
--I can't take it...
--I-Ino-<i>sempai</i>!

00:08:22.836 --> 00:08:26.507
Riri suggested this bathroom
as a good place to disguise.

00:08:28.425 --> 00:08:30.636
I-I can only buy ten copies at a time, right?

00:08:30.636 --> 00:08:32.471
Th-That's right.

00:08:32.471 --> 00:08:35.807
I've seen that hat multiple times at the event!

00:08:36.725 --> 00:08:40.062
--I remember that hat, too...
--Yikes!

00:08:40.062 --> 00:08:42.898
There weren't many girls for me,
so you stood out.

00:08:42.898 --> 00:08:46.235
Chiko, so you were here since the morning!

00:08:46.235 --> 00:08:48.529
D-Don't get it all mixed up.

00:08:48.529 --> 00:08:51.073
I wouldn't be here if my big sister wasn't!

00:08:51.073 --> 00:08:53.784
Nice! Chiko's hot and cold act in person!

00:08:53.784 --> 00:08:56.912
Why are you being like that now?

00:08:56.912 --> 00:08:59.915
Anyway, how many CDs did you buy...?

00:08:59.915 --> 00:09:01.667
"1. A Tart Feeling"
"2. Aim For It! No. 1 Curry!"

00:09:02.793 --> 00:09:04.044
--Miss Chiko...
--N-No!

00:09:04.044 --> 00:09:06.505
This is all for my big sister, too!

00:09:09.925 --> 00:09:12.719
If you could shake hands
with Roko-<i>sempai </i>all day,

00:09:12.719 --> 00:09:15.597
would you consider buying 500 more?

00:09:15.597 --> 00:09:18.392
The whole day... for 500 copies...?!

00:09:18.392 --> 00:09:20.644
That's enough of that, you two!

00:09:20.644 --> 00:09:22.813
I love, love meat...

00:09:22.813 --> 00:09:25.774
--I love, love meat...
--You, too...

00:09:25.774 --> 00:09:28.777
What? How to fire up your crowd?

00:09:28.777 --> 00:09:30.529
I get that you're struggling,

00:09:30.529 --> 00:09:33.699
but even I can't come up with
something like that the very last minute.

00:09:33.699 --> 00:09:36.285
We also started out performing in parks

00:09:36.285 --> 00:09:40.205
with barely any fans
and worked our way this far.

00:09:41.206 --> 00:09:42.791
Right...

00:09:50.757 --> 00:09:52.134
But...

00:09:52.134 --> 00:09:53.844
But?

00:09:53.844 --> 00:09:58.140
If you say, "Big sister Chiko, I love you!"

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:00.684
then I'll give you more advice?

00:10:00.684 --> 00:10:03.020
Harassment?! I'm the big sister!

00:10:05.731 --> 00:10:10.152
Nice! I see new customers
and the draw isn't that bad.

00:10:10.152 --> 00:10:13.655
Now the question is,
how will you steal their hearts?

00:10:13.655 --> 00:10:16.074
Good luck, Fruit Tart!

00:10:17.117 --> 00:10:18.076
All right!

00:10:18.076 --> 00:10:22.039
We will now start the afternoon half
of Fruit Tart's mini concert

00:10:22.039 --> 00:10:24.124
to celebrate their CD release!

00:10:27.127 --> 00:10:29.671
Listen, big sister.

00:10:29.671 --> 00:10:32.257
The idols don't fire up the concert.

00:10:32.257 --> 00:10:35.469
The idols have to get fired up
together with their fans.

00:10:35.469 --> 00:10:38.055
So when you talk to them,

00:10:38.055 --> 00:10:43.435
don't go for a punchline like a comedian,
go for a fun conversation instead.

00:10:43.435 --> 00:10:47.814
A fun conversation? The more I think about it...

00:10:47.814 --> 00:10:51.360
How should we know?! We all...

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:53.779
...don't have any friends!

00:10:53.779 --> 00:10:57.157
What the heck are we supposed to do?!

00:10:57.157 --> 00:10:59.117
I'm Nua Nakamachi, a second year in high school!

00:10:59.117 --> 00:11:02.079
My birthday is January 1st
and my blood type's AB.

00:11:02.079 --> 00:11:04.873
I'm 146 cm and weigh 36 kg!

00:11:04.873 --> 00:11:07.000
I love hot things!

00:11:14.341 --> 00:11:16.426
<i>Dropout Idol Fruit Tart</i>!

00:11:18.220 --> 00:11:20.055
Wh-What's going on?

00:11:20.055 --> 00:11:22.391
They're all terribly nervous...

00:11:22.391 --> 00:11:25.102
Are they gonna be okay?

00:11:25.102 --> 00:11:29.147
If we don't sell at least 1,000 copies of
the CD today, things are going to be tough.

00:11:29.147 --> 00:11:30.732
What?!

00:11:30.732 --> 00:11:33.402
Maybe that really pressured them...

00:11:33.402 --> 00:11:36.488
They're making the audience nervous, too!

00:11:36.488 --> 00:11:38.782
Excuse me, Miss!

00:11:38.782 --> 00:11:40.534
Miss...?

00:11:41.702 --> 00:11:42.870
Hey!

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:45.747
What is this gathering about?

00:11:45.747 --> 00:11:46.957
Some kind of event?

00:11:46.957 --> 00:11:49.334
S-Such a breathtaking little girl!

00:11:49.334 --> 00:11:51.503
If I start talking to her...

00:11:51.503 --> 00:11:53.714
Oh no... I'll get arrested!

00:11:53.714 --> 00:11:55.215
"Court case"

00:11:55.424 --> 00:11:58.760
Hey, what's going on with you, Miss?

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:00.512
I-It's n-nothing!

00:12:00.512 --> 00:12:02.514
I'm not anyone suspicious, either.

00:12:02.514 --> 00:12:05.392
This is an event hosted by
an idol group called Fruit Tart!

00:12:05.392 --> 00:12:06.810
Idol?

00:12:08.145 --> 00:12:11.356
Oh, no wonder they're all very cute.

00:12:11.356 --> 00:12:12.274
That's right!

00:12:12.274 --> 00:12:16.528
Fruit Tart was formed to prevent
the demolition of Mouse House,

00:12:16.528 --> 00:12:20.199
their company dorm in Higashi-Koganei,
where they're based!

00:12:20.199 --> 00:12:23.660
Oh! I'm Tone Honmachi,
their assistant, by the way.

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:25.621
Nice to meet you!

00:12:25.621 --> 00:12:26.955
Creep.

00:12:26.955 --> 00:12:28.582
D-Darn it...

00:12:28.582 --> 00:12:32.920
All I gathered was that
you're Fruit Tart's assistant.

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:35.756
So tell me, what's their appeal?

00:12:35.756 --> 00:12:37.925
--What?
--Their songs?

00:12:39.051 --> 00:12:40.719
Well...

00:12:40.719 --> 00:12:41.720
That's...

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:43.222
That's?

00:12:43.222 --> 00:12:45.599
No, never mind.

00:12:45.599 --> 00:12:46.517
What?

00:12:46.517 --> 00:12:49.478
You'll understand if you watch their show...

00:12:49.478 --> 00:12:51.730
Fruit Tart's appeal!

00:12:53.315 --> 00:12:55.609
Hey, what's going on?

00:12:55.609 --> 00:12:56.902
Sing for us!

00:12:56.902 --> 00:12:59.238
--What's going on?!
--What's going on with them?

00:12:59.238 --> 00:13:00.489
Something feels off.

00:13:00.489 --> 00:13:02.783
They were full of energy in the morning.

00:13:02.783 --> 00:13:04.201
You've got this!

00:13:04.201 --> 00:13:05.953
Wh-What should we do...?

00:13:05.953 --> 00:13:08.163
H-Hello, everyone!

00:13:08.163 --> 00:13:11.083
Everyone! We actually...

00:13:11.083 --> 00:13:12.668
...have really small bladders!

00:13:12.668 --> 00:13:14.044
What?!

00:13:15.504 --> 00:13:17.047
No! That's not what I meant!

00:13:17.047 --> 00:13:19.967
We're all dropouts in our own way...!

00:13:19.967 --> 00:13:23.804
I'm a newcomer who was
the backup winner at the audition.

00:13:23.804 --> 00:13:26.223
Roko-<i>sempai </i>is a former child actor.

00:13:26.223 --> 00:13:28.600
Hayu is a former musician.

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:31.186
Nina-<i>sempai </i>is a former fashion model.

00:13:32.604 --> 00:13:34.523
Hemo is...

00:13:34.523 --> 00:13:36.608
Hemo is...

00:13:36.608 --> 00:13:38.902
...a young girl full of hope, so I'm sorry.

00:13:38.902 --> 00:13:40.404
Ino-<i>sempai</i>!

00:13:40.404 --> 00:13:42.489
Hey! What about us?!

00:13:44.575 --> 00:13:49.496
But the point is, we,
dropouts are on stage right now!

00:13:49.496 --> 00:13:51.498
That alone makes me so happy!

00:13:51.498 --> 00:13:54.001
And I'm forever grateful for you all!

00:13:54.001 --> 00:13:56.044
--Inocchi!
--Ino-<i>sempai</i>!

00:13:56.044 --> 00:13:58.005
--Ino...
--Ino!

00:13:58.005 --> 00:14:01.717
A higher-up told us to fire up the show,

00:14:01.717 --> 00:14:03.468
but we didn't know what to do!

00:14:03.468 --> 00:14:05.470
A higher-up? Who? Me?!

00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:07.806
Well, we could wear less clothes...

00:14:07.806 --> 00:14:09.808
That's totally possible!

00:14:09.808 --> 00:14:10.851
Sexual harassment?!

00:14:10.851 --> 00:14:12.853
That's the last resort, Ino!

00:14:12.853 --> 00:14:15.105
I-Ino-<i>sempai</i>!

00:14:15.105 --> 00:14:18.233
We've still got a long way to go
with our singing, dancing, and talking...

00:14:18.233 --> 00:14:21.820
What else can we do to
get to know each other better...?

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:23.363
Um...

00:14:24.531 --> 00:14:25.866
Um...

00:14:25.866 --> 00:14:28.493
Um, what exactly should I do?

00:14:28.493 --> 00:14:30.704
You spoke without thinking it through?!

00:14:30.704 --> 00:14:34.583
But I have no idea how to make friends!

00:14:34.583 --> 00:14:36.668
Me neither.

00:14:36.668 --> 00:14:38.003
N-Nina-<i>sempai</i>!

00:14:38.003 --> 00:14:39.838
Wh-What? M-Me?!

00:14:39.838 --> 00:14:41.173
Then Roko-<i>sempai</i>!

00:14:41.173 --> 00:14:43.717
Oh, wait! Where is she?!

00:14:43.717 --> 00:14:44.801
Hey!

00:14:44.801 --> 00:14:46.428
I'm right here.

00:14:47.596 --> 00:14:50.057
I-I can't think of anything right now,

00:14:50.057 --> 00:14:53.852
so we'll be doing whatever we can
to the best of our ability right now!

00:14:53.852 --> 00:14:56.980
If you'd like, please get fired up with us!

00:14:56.980 --> 00:14:59.274
That's fine by us!

00:14:59.274 --> 00:15:01.527
You've got this, Fruit Tart!

00:15:01.527 --> 00:15:02.694
Chiko!

00:15:02.694 --> 00:15:04.696
--Chiko!
--You've got this!

00:15:08.867 --> 00:15:10.077
Ino!

00:15:10.077 --> 00:15:11.328
Yes!

00:15:11.328 --> 00:15:13.622
Now, everybody, please enjoy!

00:15:13.622 --> 00:15:15.457
Our new song!

00:15:15.457 --> 00:15:18.377
"Aim For It! No. 1 Curry!"

00:15:21.171 --> 00:15:24.758
♬ Curry highway full speed ahead! Hey! ♬

00:15:24.758 --> 00:15:27.511
♬ India! Myanmar! Thailand! Sri Lanka! ♬

00:15:27.511 --> 00:15:28.262
♬ Fire! ♬

00:15:28.262 --> 00:15:31.139
♬ Nepal! Singapore! England! Japan! ♬

00:15:31.139 --> 00:15:31.890
♬ Fire! ♬

00:15:31.890 --> 00:15:35.394
♬ So happy! So fun! So delicious and happy! ♬

00:15:35.394 --> 00:15:37.813
♬ Curry rice and curry bowls
are different things! ♬

00:15:37.813 --> 00:15:38.689
What?!

00:15:38.689 --> 00:15:40.482
What... What is this song?

00:15:40.482 --> 00:15:41.692
--Amazing...
--What?!

00:15:41.692 --> 00:15:43.819
You've done it, Fruit Tart!

00:15:43.819 --> 00:15:45.237
This is so moving!

00:15:45.237 --> 00:15:46.780
What?!

00:15:46.780 --> 00:15:49.324
Th-That?! Are you kidding me?

00:15:49.324 --> 00:15:50.993
Of course!

00:15:50.993 --> 00:15:53.412
Look carefully at the fans.

00:15:53.412 --> 00:15:57.040
They're dancing along, going with the rhythm.

00:15:57.040 --> 00:15:58.375
Y-You're right!

00:15:58.375 --> 00:16:00.377
That's not a common sight.

00:16:00.377 --> 00:16:03.964
Now that's the true power of idols.

00:16:03.964 --> 00:16:07.467
Well, they say songs can move people's hearts...

00:16:07.467 --> 00:16:10.262
♬ India! Myanmar! Thailand! Sri Lanka! ♬

00:16:10.262 --> 00:16:10.971
♬ Fire! ♬

00:16:10.971 --> 00:16:14.516
--♬ Nepal! Singapore! England! Japan! Fire! ♬
--Isn't this more like brainwashing
or something awful like that?

00:16:14.516 --> 00:16:18.061
♬ So happy! So fun! So delicious and happy! ♬

00:16:18.061 --> 00:16:21.648
♬ Curry rice and curry bowls
are different things! ♬

00:16:21.648 --> 00:16:25.861
♬ Curry highway full speed ahead! Hey! ♬

00:16:38.832 --> 00:16:39.958
But...

00:16:39.958 --> 00:16:41.460
We did it!

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:43.754
We did it girls, we sold 1,000 copies!

00:16:43.754 --> 00:16:44.755
What?!

00:16:44.755 --> 00:16:45.797
Really?!

00:16:45.797 --> 00:16:48.675
An elementary school student bought 300 of them!

00:16:48.675 --> 00:16:49.801
What?!

00:16:49.801 --> 00:16:50.928
Three hundred?!

00:16:50.928 --> 00:16:52.679
A rich elementary school kid?!

00:16:55.724 --> 00:16:57.601
It's so heavy!

00:16:57.601 --> 00:17:00.479
Wh-What kind of kid are they...?

00:17:00.479 --> 00:17:01.522
Who knows.

00:17:01.522 --> 00:17:05.108
They did have that rich person aura to them.

00:17:05.108 --> 00:17:07.236
Anyway...

00:17:07.236 --> 00:17:10.239
We're going to go feast on beef as promised!

00:17:10.239 --> 00:17:11.406
Let's live it up!

00:17:11.406 --> 00:17:13.200
Beef?!

00:17:17.287 --> 00:17:19.581
Go on, eat all you like.

00:17:19.581 --> 00:17:21.750
Come on, don't be shy.

00:17:21.750 --> 00:17:23.836
Yeah... We knew.

00:18:54.551 --> 00:18:55.761
Let's try this again!

00:18:55.761 --> 00:18:58.222
You've all been in a bad mood
since the beef bowl,

00:18:58.222 --> 00:19:01.266
so we'll redo the after-party.

00:19:01.266 --> 00:19:02.851
Titled!

00:19:02.851 --> 00:19:05.312
<i>Dropout Idol Fruit Tart </i>Episode 9:

00:19:05.312 --> 00:19:09.024
"Throw a cute and funny
after-party like an idol!"

00:19:09.024 --> 00:19:10.692
"Okonomiyaki"
"Tone"

00:19:11.818 --> 00:19:13.153
T-Tone?!

00:19:13.153 --> 00:19:14.571
Why aren't you all in your swimsuits?!

00:19:14.571 --> 00:19:15.864
What do you mean?!

00:19:15.864 --> 00:19:19.076
Well, I heard it's a cute and
sexy episode, so I just assumed...

00:19:19.076 --> 00:19:20.744
Not sexy!

00:19:20.827 --> 00:19:21.495
"Certified Beer Expert"

00:19:21.495 --> 00:19:24.414
"Certified Beer Expert"
But it's been a while since we had <i>okonomiyaki</i>!

00:19:24.414 --> 00:19:28.961
We rarely go out to eat,
so we never get to eat it!

00:19:28.961 --> 00:19:31.922
Don't tell me we're limited to 500 yen each.

00:19:31.922 --> 00:19:33.924
Like with the beef bowls last time.

00:19:33.924 --> 00:19:35.467
H-How rude!

00:19:35.467 --> 00:19:37.469
That's why we're making this an episode!

00:19:37.469 --> 00:19:39.888
To write it off as an expense!

00:19:39.888 --> 00:19:41.139
H-Hoho!

00:19:41.139 --> 00:19:44.059
Just don't dirty your precious costumes, okay?

00:19:44.059 --> 00:19:45.811
They don't pay for the cleaners!

00:19:45.811 --> 00:19:46.812
What?!

00:19:46.812 --> 00:19:48.230
Then why make us wear it?!

00:19:48.230 --> 00:19:50.065
"Roko"

00:19:50.065 --> 00:19:53.819
"Roko"
If you're that worried, I've brought
the school swimsuits just in case...

00:19:53.819 --> 00:19:56.446
"Roko"
I question your way of thinking...

00:19:56.446 --> 00:20:00.200
All right! The ones in charge
of cooking are these two!

00:20:00.200 --> 00:20:04.079
Miss Sakura and Hemo!

00:20:04.079 --> 00:20:06.748
And I've got these for the eating specialists!

00:20:06.748 --> 00:20:09.793
Tone's special aprons!

00:20:10.711 --> 00:20:13.130
Way to go, daughter of the <i>okonomiyaki </i>joint!

00:20:13.130 --> 00:20:16.216
Now we don't need to worry
about ruining our costumes...

00:20:16.216 --> 00:20:17.342
Huh?

00:20:17.342 --> 00:20:20.053
Sorry, I was short one.

00:20:20.053 --> 00:20:21.889
Liar.

00:20:21.889 --> 00:20:24.975
All right, Hemo, let's get started!

00:20:24.975 --> 00:20:27.186
Yes, Ino-<i>sempai</i>!

00:20:27.186 --> 00:20:29.980
Thanks for helping, Hemo!

00:20:29.980 --> 00:20:33.859
Not a problem! I've actually
been studying up on cooking!

00:20:33.859 --> 00:20:37.196
Nowadays, housework is divided equally!

00:20:38.405 --> 00:20:41.992
All right! Now let's start
making <i>okonomiyaki </i>together!

00:20:41.992 --> 00:20:43.202
Okay!

00:20:43.202 --> 00:20:45.996
Pour a thin layer of the batter in the grill.

00:20:45.996 --> 00:20:48.582
Mix all the ingredients in the bowl.

00:20:48.582 --> 00:20:51.293
Layer the cabbage and ingredients
and top it off with an egg!

00:20:51.293 --> 00:20:54.838
Try to incorporate as much air as possible
and gently mold it to shape!

00:20:54.838 --> 00:20:56.507
What?!

00:20:56.507 --> 00:20:57.758
Hemo...

00:20:57.758 --> 00:20:59.134
Ino-<i>sempai</i>...

00:20:59.134 --> 00:21:00.177
Don't tell me...

00:21:00.177 --> 00:21:02.346
Shoot! This is bad!

00:21:02.346 --> 00:21:06.350
The Osaka-style vs Hiroshima-style,
which is better dispute broke out!

00:21:06.350 --> 00:21:08.310
"Osaka!!!"

00:21:08.310 --> 00:21:10.270
"Hiroshima!!!"

00:21:10.479 --> 00:21:12.356
My dad is from Osaka,

00:21:12.356 --> 00:21:14.483
and my mom is from Hiroshima,

00:21:14.483 --> 00:21:17.402
so this dispute caused a great rift
between their families

00:21:17.402 --> 00:21:19.112
right at the beginning of their marriage!

00:21:19.112 --> 00:21:21.823
What were your parents thinking?!

00:21:21.823 --> 00:21:24.326
We've split evenly, Roko-<i>sempai</i>.

00:21:24.326 --> 00:21:27.120
Can't believe you're on that side, too, Nina.

00:21:27.120 --> 00:21:30.958
How could you when you both have
great Osaka-style figures!

00:21:30.958 --> 00:21:32.626
What are you implying about me?!

00:21:32.626 --> 00:21:36.505
That's right! Osaka-style is fluffy
and the batter is flavorful!

00:21:36.505 --> 00:21:40.425
Hiroshima-style brings out the flavor of
each ingredient and is simply the best!

00:21:40.425 --> 00:21:42.344
All right, then.

00:21:42.344 --> 00:21:44.972
We'll have to ask the <i>okonomiyaki </i>specialist!

00:21:44.972 --> 00:21:46.223
M-Me...?!

00:21:46.223 --> 00:21:49.309
What do you think as a half-Osaka
and half-Hiroshima person?!

00:21:49.309 --> 00:21:50.936
Don't say it like that!

00:21:50.936 --> 00:21:53.730
U-Um, I think...

00:21:53.730 --> 00:21:54.731
You think...

00:21:54.731 --> 00:21:56.650
I personally like <i>monjayaki</i>.

00:21:56.650 --> 00:21:57.818
Tokyo-style?!

00:21:57.818 --> 00:21:59.027
Actually...

00:21:59.027 --> 00:22:02.698
I got hooked ever since I tried it
when I moved here...

00:22:02.698 --> 00:22:06.159
But I love both Osaka and Hiroshima-style, too!

00:22:06.159 --> 00:22:09.246
They're still the most cost-effective dish
that gets stretched out to the max

00:22:09.246 --> 00:22:11.248
just with flour and cabbage!

00:22:11.248 --> 00:22:13.375
You probably shouldn't say that too much.

00:22:14.251 --> 00:22:16.587
They're all delicious and they're all great!

00:22:16.587 --> 00:22:18.547
Come on, this is a celebration.

00:22:18.547 --> 00:22:20.340
Let's all get along.

00:22:20.340 --> 00:22:22.050
You're right.

00:22:22.050 --> 00:22:23.802
Let's finish it off!

00:22:23.802 --> 00:22:24.845
Yes!

00:22:24.845 --> 00:22:26.221
--With mayo!
--With mustard-mayo!

00:22:26.221 --> 00:22:27.431
What?!

00:22:27.431 --> 00:22:28.849
Seriously?!

00:22:31.351 --> 00:22:32.603
Tone!

00:22:32.603 --> 00:22:34.855
Will you accept this?

00:22:34.855 --> 00:22:38.734
Th-This is an autographed copy of the CD?!

00:22:38.734 --> 00:22:43.322
We wanted to thank you for everything
you've done, not just for today.

00:22:43.322 --> 00:22:44.531
"1. A Tart Feeling"
"2. Aim For It! No. 1 Curry!"

00:22:44.531 --> 00:22:48.869
"1. A Tart Feeling"
"2. Aim For It! No. 1 Curry!"
We don't have money, so we can
only give you something like that.

00:22:48.869 --> 00:22:50.287
We appreciate you.

00:22:50.287 --> 00:22:51.955
Thanks, Tonecchi!

00:22:51.955 --> 00:22:53.290
You take care of us!

00:22:53.290 --> 00:22:55.083
Thanks for your support!

00:22:57.586 --> 00:22:58.128
"Fruit Tart"

00:22:58.128 --> 00:23:02.841
"Fruit Tart"
No... This is the best gift
you could ever give me!

00:23:02.841 --> 00:23:04.968
Thanks, everyone!

00:23:04.968 --> 00:23:08.555
I know you're all at risk of the program getting
cut because of renewal season, so thanks a lot!

00:23:08.555 --> 00:23:09.389
What?

00:23:09.389 --> 00:23:10.641
Cut?

00:23:10.641 --> 00:23:12.309
Renewal season...?

00:23:12.309 --> 00:23:17.898
What?!

00:23:25.322 --> 00:23:27.074
"Preview"
Bam!

00:23:27.074 --> 00:23:30.619
"Preview"
Next on <i>Dropout Idol Fruit Tart</i>!

00:23:30.619 --> 00:23:31.828
Nua here!

00:23:31.828 --> 00:23:36.250
Hey, I only appeared announcing the episode
title and in the midpoint break this time!

00:23:36.250 --> 00:23:39.169
In fact! I barely have
any scenes next time, too!

00:23:39.169 --> 00:23:43.298
I'll just have to show Fruit Tart a thing or two
in the National Idol Championships!

00:23:43.298 --> 00:23:45.133
"Look at Us!"
<i>Dropout Idol Fruit Tart</i>!

00:23:45.133 --> 00:23:47.803
"Look at Us!"
Episode 11: "Look at Us!"

00:23:47.803 --> 00:23:50.102
"Look at Us!"
All right, see you next time!
